    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-c60e5dc9d366\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"permission-denial-literal\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"[Pp]ermission denied|PERMISSION_DENIED|\\\\bEACCES\\\\b|\\\\bEPERM\\\\b|[Oo]peration not permitted|\\\\b403\\\\b.{0,20}Forbidden\",\"path\":\".floor/transcript.jsonl\"},{\"id\":\"missing-credentials-literal\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\b401\\\\b.{0,20}Unauthorized|[Aa]uthentication (failed|required)|[Ii]nvalid (credentials|API key|token)|[Mm]issing (credentials|API key|access token)|[Nn]o credentials found|[Aa]ccess token (has )?expired\",\"path\":\".floor/transcript.jsonl\"}],\"coverage\":\"Treats a 'yes' answer as the case the constraints flag. They flag sessions whose transcript events contain literal permission-denial errors (Permission denied, EACCES, EPERM, Operation not permitted, 403 Forbidden). They also flag literal missing or invalid credential errors (401 Unauthorized, authentication failed or required, invalid or missing credentials or API key, expired access token).\",\"residual\":\"Leaving aside literal permission-denial and authentication error strings in the events, do the most recent events, read against the worker's job, show a real, unresolved blocker that only a person can clear, such as missing access, an ambiguous requirement, or a decision with irreversible consequences?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"transcript\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"cat /etc/app/secrets.yaml\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"cat: /etc/app/secrets.yaml: Permission denied\"}],\"final_message\":\"I cannot read the secrets file; please grant access.\"},{\"transcript\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"npm publish\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"npm ERR! 401 Unauthorized - invalid credentials for registry\"}],\"final_message\":\"Publishing needs a registry login.\"}],\"compliant\":{\"transcript\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"npm test\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"12 passing, 0 failing\"}],\"final_message\":\"All tests pass; the feature is done.\"}},\"rationale\":\"Literal permission-denial and authentication-failure messages in tool results are mechanically detectable in transcript.jsonl. Three things are not: whether those events are recent and still unresolved, whether a requirement is ambiguous, and whether a decision is irreversible. These depend on meaning, intent and the worker's job, so they are left for judgement.\"}",
